1
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:08,340
Hey.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:11,840
- What you guys doing?     - Monica's making us watch Old Yeller.

3
00:00:13,970 --> 00:00:17,640
Why are you guys upset? It's Old Yeller. It's a happy movie.

4
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,310
- What?     - What are you talking about?

5
00:00:20,470 --> 00:00:22,770
Come on. Happy family gets a dog.

6
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:24,560
Frontier fun!

7
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:28,270
Pheebs, what about the end?

8
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:31,610
Oh, when Yeller saves the family from the wolf and everyone's happy?

9
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:32,990
That's not the end.

10
00:00:33,150 --> 00:00:37,070
Yeah-huh. That's when my mother would shut off the TV and say, "The end."

11
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,580
What about when he has rabies?

12
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:43,120
He doesn't have rabies. He has babies.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,750
That's what my mom said.

14
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:51,550
Uh, Phoebe, I don't think she'd want you to see what's about to happen.

15
00:00:52,420 --> 00:00:54,170
Why? What's about to happen?

16
00:00:54,380 --> 00:00:56,180
I've never seen this part.

17
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:59,390
Hey, Travis, what you doing with that gun?

18
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:03,140
Oh, no.

19
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,600
No, no, Travis, put down the gun.

20
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:08,560
No, no, he's your buddy. He's your Yeller.

21
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:10,230
No! The end! The end!

22
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:16,990
Okay, what kind of a sick doggy snuff film is this?

23
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,530
∮ So no one told you life was gonna be this way ∮

24
00:01:29,070 --> 00:01:33,240
∮ Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. ∮

25
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:37,960
∮ It's like you're always stuck in second gear ∮

26
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:40,520
∮ When it hasn't been your day, ∮

27
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:43,520
∮ your week, your month, or even your year ∮

28
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:47,480
∮ but I'll be there for you ∮

29
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,310
∮ When the rain starts to pour ∮

30
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:52,430
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

31
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:54,270
∮ Like I've been there before ∮

32
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:57,280
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

33
00:01:57,280 --> 00:02:00,940
∮ 'Cause you're there for me too ∮

34
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,500
Have you guys eaten? Uh, Richard and I just finished, and we've got leftovers.

35
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:13,790
Chicken and potatoes.

36
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,710
What am I wearing?

37
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:19,840
Actually, nothing but rubber gloves.

38
00:02:25,850 --> 00:02:29,390
One of these times, you'll really be naked and we won't come over.

39
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,270
I got a leg, three breasts and a wing.

40
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:35,400
How do you find clothes that fit?

41
00:02:36,650 --> 00:02:38,740
Oh, hey, Monica? We got a question.

42
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:42,320
All right, yes, I see other women in the shower at the gym.

43
00:02:42,570 --> 00:02:43,990
And no, I don't look.

44
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:46,200
No, not that one.

45
00:02:46,450 --> 00:02:49,330
We're figuring out who to bring to the Knicks game.

46
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:52,790
Ross can't go, so it's between my friend Eric Prower, who has breath issues...

47
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:57,550
and Dan, with the poking. "Did you see that play?"

48
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:00,880
"You want more beer? Is that Spike Lee?"

49
00:03:01,050 --> 00:03:03,260
Ha, ha, okay.

50
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,970
Why don't you ask Richard?

51
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:10,140
Uh, Richard, if you had an extra ticket to the Knicks game...

52
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:16,110
and you had to choose between a friend who smelled...

53
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:20,030
and one who bruises you, who would you pick?

54
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,490
Wow.

55
00:03:21,650 --> 00:03:23,490
Being a huge Knicks fan myself...

56
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:27,740
I think you should take someone who's a huge Knicks fan.

57
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:29,660
Okay.

58
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:31,410
That's Eric.

59
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:34,830
Glad to be of help. Matches.

60
00:03:36,290 --> 00:03:38,550
I meant, why don't you take Richard to the game?

61
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:40,300
Eh.

62
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,880
What?

63
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,890
- I don't know.     - Come on!

64
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:49,560
He keeps his fingers to himself, and he's always minty fresh.

65
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:53,310
Richard's really nice. Uh, we just don't know him really well.

66
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,230
Plus, he's old...

67
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:59,980
older than some people.

68
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:03,070
But, uh, younger than some buildings.

69
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,700
So what, he's a little older. Big deal.

70
00:04:07,950 --> 00:04:09,490
He's important to me.

71
00:04:09,660 --> 00:04:12,620
If you ask him, he might take you in his Jag.

72
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:18,590
How do we say yes...

73
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:21,590
and make it seem like it's not just to ride in the cool car?

74
00:04:23,590 --> 00:04:25,260
Okay, this could be tough.

75
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:28,220
Okay, okay, okay. Monica?

76
00:04:28,390 --> 00:04:31,890
We'll bring him, but only if he takes the Jaguar.

77
00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:36,270
Ooh, you almost had it.

78
00:04:42,740 --> 00:04:44,860
No, no, you're fine. You're fine.

79
00:04:45,030 --> 00:04:46,990
- Hello, ha, ha.     - Hey.

80
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:48,820
Hi, honey. Oh.

81
00:04:49,030 --> 00:04:51,490
You are not gonna believe what happened!

82
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:54,870
We were playing on the floor, and he grabs the table...

83
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:57,080
and he pulls himself up!

84
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,670
He pulled himself up!

85
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,380
Standing man!

86
00:05:03,590 --> 00:05:07,260
I'm sorry you missed it, but I did tape it if you wanna see it.

87
00:05:07,470 --> 00:05:10,390
Uh, we know. He already did it last week.

88
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,720
You can watch our tape if you want.

89
00:05:12,890 --> 00:05:17,310
Ah, see, I don't believe this. I missed the first time of everything.

90
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:20,730
The first time he rolled over, the first time he crawled.

91
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:23,280
What else? Has he spoken? Is he driving?

92
00:05:23,530 --> 00:05:26,150
Does he have a favorite liqueur?

93
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:28,820
He is getting closer on the talking thing.

94
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:32,370
He can't quite say "mama" yet, but once he said "Yemen."

95
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:36,370
See, I don't know. I'm so sick of missing stuff.

96
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:40,170
I want him for more than a day. I want him for a whole weekend.

97
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,420
Listen. I feel...

98
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:43,000
That would be great.

99
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:48,680
Really? I had a whole speech prepared.

100
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,970
Oh, shoot, that would've been fun.

101
00:05:53,850 --> 00:05:55,390
Oh, look, did you just see that?

102
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:58,190
Did you see? He just waved! He just waved!

103
00:05:58,350 --> 00:06:00,690
He's never waved before!

104
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,150
Yes, he has. Very good.

105
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:08,320
- Hey.     - Hey, Pheebs. What you got there?

106
00:06:08,570 --> 00:06:12,450
Love Story, Brian's Song and Terms of Endearment.

107
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:15,330
Wow, all you need now is The Killing Fields...

108
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:18,120
and some guacamole, and you got yourself a party!

109
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:22,460
I talked to my grandma about the Old Yeller incident...

110
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:26,460
and she said my mom used to not show us the ends of sad movies...

111
00:06:26,710 --> 00:06:29,380
to shield us from the pain and sadness.

112
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:32,180
You know, before she killed herself.

113
00:06:33,890 --> 00:06:35,850
- Hey.     - Hey.

114
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:38,230
Where's Richard? Did you ditch him?

115
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:41,480
After we stole his lunch money and gave him a wedgie.

116
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:45,270
What's the matter with you? He's parking the car.

117
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:49,990
- Did you guys have fun?     - Your boyfriend is so cool.

118
00:06:50,150 --> 00:06:54,200
He let us drive his Jaguar. Joey for 12 blocks. Me for 15.

119
00:06:54,370 --> 00:06:55,910
Wow.

120
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:57,580
He must like you best.

121
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:01,580
Oh, what about when he tipped the guy who showed us to our seats?

122
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,710
You never even saw the money.

123
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:06,670
Hey, Chandler, thanks for showing us to our seats.

124
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:10,800
Ha, ha, you're welcome. Hey, Joey, thanks for parking the car.

125
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:12,680
No problem, ha, ha.

126
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:16,180
- Hey, Chandler...     - I think they get it.

127
00:07:18,810 --> 00:07:20,020
There's the man!

128
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,980
Hey.

129
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:23,900
- Hey, you're getting better.     - Huh? Ha, ha.

130
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:26,110
I'm gonna keep this.

131
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:28,070
Okay.

132
00:07:28,230 --> 00:07:29,320
He kept my dollar.

133
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:38,160
Your first weekend without Ben. What are you doing?

134
00:07:38,370 --> 00:07:40,290
Ah, we're going to colonial Williamsburg.

135
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:44,960
A woman I went to college with is the first female blacksmith there.

136
00:07:45,210 --> 00:07:48,380
They're a little behind the times in colonial Williamsburg.

137
00:07:48,550 --> 00:07:52,090
Ha, ha. Well, look, I better go before Mommy starts weeping.

138
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:55,260
- We love you.     - Bye, Mommy.

139
00:07:55,510 --> 00:07:57,300
Have a good time.

140
00:07:58,180 --> 00:07:59,430
Okay, Ben.

141
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:00,680
- Ross.     - Yeah?

142
00:08:00,850 --> 00:08:01,930
Look.

143
00:08:09,070 --> 00:08:11,650
Joey, do you know we can see you from here?

144
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:15,780
How come Richard looks cooler with one of these?

145
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:18,910
You may wanna light it and lose the spatula.

146
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,710
It's cute, you trying to be more like Richard.

147
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:25,670
Not like him, per se.

148
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,040
Just not unlike him.

149
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,810
It's the artist formerly known as Chandler.

150
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:45,230
I'm just trying something here, you know?

151
00:08:45,390 --> 00:08:47,150
Why didn't you grow a mustache?

152
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:48,520
Oh, we flipped for it.

153
00:08:48,690 --> 00:08:50,570
I got the cigar, he got the mustache.

154
00:08:52,110 --> 00:08:53,860
If we both grew them, we'd look like dorks.

155
00:08:55,570 --> 00:08:58,200
You really sidestepped that land mine.

156
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:01,540
I promised Richard we'd meet downstairs.

157
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:02,790
You're meeting Richard?

158
00:09:02,950 --> 00:09:04,660
- Ranger game.     - Didn't he tell you?

159
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:08,210
He said he was going out with the guys. I didn't know that was you.

160
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:09,580
You hear that?

161
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,750
- We're the guys!     - We're the guys!

162
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:15,510
With that mustache, he reminds me of Aunt Sylvia.

163
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,010
Thank you!

164
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:25,090

165
00:09:26,060 --> 00:09:28,560
- Hi, we're visiting.     - Yay.

166
00:09:28,730 --> 00:09:31,770
It's Ben and his dada.

167
00:09:32,150 --> 00:09:34,110
Dada.

168
00:09:34,610 --> 00:09:36,990
- Can you say "dada"?     - Aw.

169
00:09:37,150 --> 00:09:40,280
I'm telling your mommies you said it, so you might as well.

170
00:09:40,490 --> 00:09:42,080
- No luck, huh?     - No.

171
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:44,540
A while ago, I got a "seh" out of him...

172
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:49,670
which I thought might turn into "seh-condary caregiver," but...

173
00:09:52,630 --> 00:09:55,380
Would you, uh, hold him for a sec? I gotta take this off.

174
00:09:55,590 --> 00:09:58,470
- Oh, yeah, sure, okay.     - There we go.

175
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:05,520
What are you doing?

176
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,640
I'm holding Ben.

177
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:11,560
Yeah, well, he's a baby, not a bomb.

178
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:13,610
Okay.

179
00:10:13,770 --> 00:10:15,570
Hold him like you'd hold a football.

180
00:10:16,190 --> 00:10:18,610
This is how I would hold a football.

181
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:21,030
Here. Here. There we go.

182
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:25,580
Sorry, I'm not very good with babies. I haven't been around them.

183
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:27,910
- I mean, you know, since I was one.     - Ha, ha.

184
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:30,960
- It's all right. No big deal.     - Really?

185
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:34,040
You'll feel different when it's our baby.

186
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:35,960
- What?     - What?

187
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,670
You think about stuff like that?

188
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,590
Uh, yeah. I mean...

189
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:46,180
Actually, I kind of think that we'll have two babies.

190
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:49,980
Two babies?

191
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:52,230
You know, a boy and a girl.

192
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:55,820
Hopefully, the girl will come first, so Ben won't feel competitive.

193
00:10:58,650 --> 00:11:00,400
Then what's gonna happen?

194
00:11:00,570 --> 00:11:04,660
We won't wanna raise kids in the city, so we'll move to Scarsdale.

195
00:11:04,830 --> 00:11:06,410
Scar... Uh-huh.

196
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:10,040
We'll be far enough from our parents so we don't have to see them...

197
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:12,670
but close enough that they can babysit.

198
00:11:12,830 --> 00:11:17,090
And yes, I know the taxes are a little higher than Nassau County...

199
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:19,340
but the school system's great.

200
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:22,050
Wow! Ha, ha.

201
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,890
Wow, that's great! Great!

202
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,720
- Okay, wow! You know what?     - Hmm?

203
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:30,600
I'm off my break now. So, uh...

204
00:11:30,770 --> 00:11:32,730
Um, here. You take this.

205
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:34,900
And, um...

206
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:38,150
I'm gonna go pour these very nice people some coffee.

207
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:39,440
Okay.

208
00:11:39,610 --> 00:11:41,650
Look at that. I don't have a pot.

209
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:44,280
I don't have a pot. Maybe I've got one at home.

210
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:46,870
Or in Scarsdale. Hey, is that a door?

211
00:11:47,030 --> 00:11:48,620
Rach.

212
00:11:52,870 --> 00:11:55,080
- Hey.     - Hey, Pheebs. What's happening?

213
00:11:55,250 --> 00:11:59,550
Oh, okay, murder, cancer, soccer teams eating each other in the Andes.

214
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:03,260
- You watched the movies?     - Uh-huh.

215
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:06,090
What is happening to the world?

216
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,470
I mean... No, no, because E.T. Leaves...

217
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:12,350
and Rocky loses. Charlotte dies.

218
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,060
Charlotte who?

219
00:12:14,310 --> 00:12:15,600
With the web. The spider.

220
00:12:15,770 --> 00:12:17,980
She dies. She has babies and dies.

221
00:12:18,190 --> 00:12:21,280
It's like, "Welcome home from the hospital." Thud!

222
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,030
You wanna feel better?

223
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:26,610
- Yeah.     - Okay.

224
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:29,870
Here. Watch this.

225
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,700
It's a Wonderful Life. Yes, I've heard of this.

226
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,500
So you can't lose. It's there in the title.

227
00:12:35,750 --> 00:12:37,420
Wonderfulness is baked right in.

228
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:40,090
I fell for that with Pride of the Yankees.

229
00:12:40,250 --> 00:12:42,380
I thought I'd see a film about Yankee pride.

230
00:12:42,590 --> 00:12:45,720
And boom! The guy gets Lou Gehrig's disease.

231
00:12:46,470 --> 00:12:51,720
Uh, the guy was Lou Gehrig. Didn't you kind of see it coming?

232
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:56,350
Watch that. It'll restore all your faith in humanity.

233
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:59,230
Hey, big guy. Game time.

234
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,280
- Hey! Be right there!     - There's a game?

235
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:05,610
I just got my Pik-Up Stiks back from the shop.

236
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:08,740
Bring your nerves of steel.

237
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:13,040
It's the basketball playoffs.

238
00:13:13,290 --> 00:13:17,750
Um, I appreciate this, but you don't have to hang out with them for me.

239
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,460
They have each other.

240
00:13:19,630 --> 00:13:21,840
Oh, no, honey. I mean, don't worry.

241
00:13:22,050 --> 00:13:25,970
I like hanging out with them. They're different than my other friends.

242
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:30,220
They don't start sentences with "You know who just died shoveling snow?"

243
00:13:31,430 --> 00:13:33,640
All right, that's great. Then just go.

244
00:13:34,390 --> 00:13:35,480
Go Knicks!

245
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,940
- Uh, it's the college playoffs.     - Oh.

246
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:40,520
- Then, go Vassar!     - Uh, they're not in it.

247
00:13:40,690 --> 00:13:43,570
- Okay, then just go.     - Okay.

248
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:46,650
Ugh, why does this bother me so much?

249
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:51,700
I'm not one of those people who wants to spend 24 hours a day together.

250
00:13:51,870 --> 00:13:53,160
Sure.

251
00:13:53,330 --> 00:13:56,500
He just doesn't have much free time. What do I do?

252
00:13:56,660 --> 00:14:00,630
Does it matter? You'll just die or divorce or blow your pet's head off.

253
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,710
- Ugh!     - Me too!

254
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:09,340
Rachel, I got a question. Richard made plans again with the guys...

255
00:14:09,510 --> 00:14:11,470
Ross made plans for the century.

256
00:14:11,640 --> 00:14:15,640
I'm gonna go read Cosmo. Maybe there's something helpful in it.

257
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:20,600
If not, I can learn how to do a bikini wax with leftover Christmas candles.

258
00:14:22,190 --> 00:14:23,520
Okay.

259
00:14:23,690 --> 00:14:25,530
What happened back there?

260
00:14:25,780 --> 00:14:27,530
I don't know. You tell me.

261
00:14:27,740 --> 00:14:30,490
One minute I'm holding Ben, then I've got two kids...

262
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:33,660
I'm living in Scarsdale complaining about taxes!

263
00:14:33,910 --> 00:14:36,490
Well, I'm sorry. I think about stuff.

264
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:40,540
You're at work, you're assembling bones, your mind wanders.

265
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:44,380
You've planned out the next 20 years. We've dated for six weeks!

266
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:46,460
You never think about our future?

267
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:49,760
I think about whose apartment we'll sleep at tomorrow...

268
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:52,090
and where we'll have dinner next Saturday!

269
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:54,850
I do not think about our children's names!

270
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:58,810
You know what our children's names will be?

271
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:00,480
Ha, ha, no.

272
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:04,270
No, I mean, you know. I read a book, and there was a girl named Emily.

273
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:06,690
And I thought that might be good.

274
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:09,570
What was the book?

275
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:12,700
The Big Book of Children's Names.

276
00:15:13,910 --> 00:15:15,160
Okay. Ross, Ross.

277
00:15:15,330 --> 00:15:16,490
Okay, listen.

278
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:18,160
What we have is amazing.

279
00:15:18,410 --> 00:15:21,250
But I do not want everything decided for me!

280
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,040
I spent my whole life like that.

281
00:15:23,290 --> 00:15:25,920
It's what I had with Barry. That's a reason I left.

282
00:15:26,090 --> 00:15:28,090
I like not knowing right now.

283
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:32,300
Sorry if that scares you, but if you wanna be with me, deal with that!

284
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:34,260
- Okay, fine!     - Thank you!

285
00:15:34,430 --> 00:15:36,800
- We're not done!     - I didn't know that.

286
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:41,350
You're with a guy who won't stop planning his future with you.

287
00:15:41,560 --> 00:15:43,390
He knows we'll end up together.

288
00:15:43,650 --> 00:15:46,810
If that scares you, tough! You'll have to deal with that.

289
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:48,980
- I will!     - Good, because I love you!

290
00:15:49,150 --> 00:15:50,740
Oh, yeah? I love you too!

291
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,150
- That's the first time we've said that!     - Yes.

292
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:55,820
- I'm gonna kiss you!     - You better!

293
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:03,580
- Hey.     - Hey.

294
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:05,330
Oh, thanks for the great movie tip.

295
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:07,420
- Did you like it?     - Oh, yeah.

296
00:16:07,590 --> 00:16:11,170
I don't know if I was happier when George Bailey destroyed the business...

297
00:16:11,340 --> 00:16:15,260
or, um, Donna Reed cried or when the pharmacist made his ear bleed.

298
00:16:17,010 --> 00:16:19,970
I'll give you the ear thing, but wasn't the ending wonderful?

299
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:22,310
I didn't watch it. I was too depressed.

300
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:24,810
It kept getting worse! It should've been called:

301
00:16:25,060 --> 00:16:29,360
"It's a Sucky Life, And Just When You Think It Can't Suck Anymore, It Does!"

302
00:16:32,110 --> 00:16:33,530
Kick, save! And...

303
00:16:33,780 --> 00:16:35,030
denied!

304
00:16:35,780 --> 00:16:39,700
He gets it back. Pass to the middle, lines it up and bam!

305
00:16:39,870 --> 00:16:40,950
Yes!

306
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:44,290
Could that shot be any prettier?

307
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,500
Man, you are incredible.

308
00:16:46,670 --> 00:16:48,460
We had a table in college.

309
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,960
Oh, really? I didn't know they had foosball in the 1800s.

310
00:16:52,760 --> 00:16:55,840
Nice mustache. At puberty, that thing will really kick in.

311
00:17:00,850 --> 00:17:04,480
Not to sound too Florence Henderson, but dinner's on the table.

312
00:17:04,730 --> 00:17:05,810
One more point.

313
00:17:08,900 --> 00:17:10,060
Score!

314
00:17:11,610 --> 00:17:13,190
- Now can we go?     - Uh...

315
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:15,900
That's why we don't let her play.

316
00:17:18,280 --> 00:17:20,950
- Is everything all right?     - Mm-hm.

317
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,200
Uh-oh.

318
00:17:22,370 --> 00:17:24,700
Oh, hey, don't be mad at him. It's our fault.

319
00:17:24,870 --> 00:17:26,870
I'm sorry we've been hogging his time.

320
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:29,210
He's just really great to hang out with.

321
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:30,630
- Well...     - No, seriously.

322
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:34,340
We just talked about this. He is so much cooler than our dads.

323
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:39,510
Our dads are okay and all, but Richard is just...

324
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,890
Ow, ow, ow. What are you kicking me for?

325
00:17:42,930 --> 00:17:45,980
Huh? I'm trying to talk here.

326
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:50,350
Uh, you guys see me as a dad?

327
00:17:50,520 --> 00:17:52,320
- Oh, yeah.     - No!

328
00:17:53,610 --> 00:17:54,690
No.

329
00:17:56,110 --> 00:18:00,240
You're just clearly not familiar with our young persons' vernacular.

330
00:18:00,490 --> 00:18:03,830
When we say "dad," we mean "buddy."

331
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:06,540
- We mean "pal."     - Uh-huh, yeah.

332
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:09,330
No, seriously. Joey's my dad.

333
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:14,090
Monica's my dad.

334
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:17,340
I've even got some dads down at work.

335
00:18:17,720 --> 00:18:18,800
That's fine.

336
00:18:18,970 --> 00:18:23,300
Well, your other dad and I are gonna go have a romantic evening.

337
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,600
I'll just see you kids around.

338
00:18:25,850 --> 00:18:27,140
Nighty-night.

339
00:18:27,310 --> 00:18:30,230
- You're not a dad!     - You're not a dad!

340
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,650
I can't believe you got us into trouble.

341
00:18:38,530 --> 00:18:39,740
So are you okay?

342
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:41,910
Yeah.

343
00:18:42,070 --> 00:18:43,200
Just...

344
00:18:43,370 --> 00:18:45,830
I feel like I'm about a hundred.

345
00:18:46,450 --> 00:18:49,160
I thought I was just one of the guys.

346
00:18:49,750 --> 00:18:50,960
Come here.

347
00:18:51,210 --> 00:18:54,040
I'll make you feel like one of the guys.

348
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:59,760
Mm.

349
00:18:59,930 --> 00:19:02,930
For a really cool guy, you suck at foosball.

350
00:19:03,930 --> 00:19:05,850
I was killing them.

351
00:19:06,010 --> 00:19:08,270
- Yeah, well they suck too.     - Ha, ha.

352
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:10,850
Hmm.

353
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:15,020
You take the poopy diaper and put it in the poopy diaper pail.

354
00:19:15,270 --> 00:19:19,360
Calling it a "poopy diaper" doesn't make this process any cuter.

355
00:19:22,990 --> 00:19:24,160
- Hello.     - It's us.

356
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:25,410
Come on up.

357
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,200
I'll get his stuff together.

358
00:19:27,370 --> 00:19:30,410
Okay, we can do this now, can't we, Ben?

359
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,920
Yes, we can.

360
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:37,880
There! I did it!

361
00:19:38,380 --> 00:19:39,880
Ha, ha, I did it!

362
00:19:40,050 --> 00:19:42,590
Ooh, look at that!

363
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:45,800
Oh, it stays on and everything.

364
00:19:46,180 --> 00:19:47,720
- Hi.     - Hi.

365
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:56,480
I'm sorry. What did you just say? Did you just say "hi"?

366
00:19:56,690 --> 00:19:59,530
Oh, my God! Ross? Ben just said hi!

367
00:19:59,690 --> 00:20:01,070
- What?     - Ben just said hi!

368
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:02,780
What, the word "hi"?

369
00:20:02,950 --> 00:20:04,780
No, my Uncle Hi.

370
00:20:05,910 --> 00:20:08,740
Great! And I missed that too. I miss everything!

371
00:20:08,990 --> 00:20:12,040
Oh, I'm sorry. I guess I just bring it out in him.

372
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:15,880
- Where is he?     - We missed you.

373
00:20:16,130 --> 00:20:19,630
We missed you so much! Come here, Ben, ha, ha.

374
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:22,300
Guess what? Ben just said his first word.

375
00:20:22,510 --> 00:20:24,340
What did he say?

376
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:26,050
Something about hi.

377
00:20:27,510 --> 00:20:30,600
- That's so exciting!     - Mommy's so proud of you!

378
00:20:30,770 --> 00:20:33,020
Hi. Hi?

379
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:35,310
You know, actually, it's more like, hi!

380
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:37,900
- Hi?     - Hi.

381
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:40,780
- Hi.     - Hi.

382
00:20:40,940 --> 00:20:42,690
This could go on for a while.

383
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:44,860
You're right. We've got a cab waiting.

384
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:46,860
Well, this was fun.

385
00:20:47,030 --> 00:20:49,990
We should do it again sometime, Ben. What do you say?

386
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:51,240
Okay.

387
00:20:51,410 --> 00:20:54,080
- All right, so I've got him?     - Tuesday.

388
00:20:54,250 --> 00:20:55,410
Bye, you guys.

389
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:57,290
- Take care.     - Bye, Ben.

390
00:20:57,460 --> 00:20:59,380
Bye.

391
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:03,760
Did he just say "bye"?

392
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:05,090
He said bye!

393
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:07,300
You said... He said bye to me!

394
00:21:07,550 --> 00:21:09,430
- Yes, he did!     - Oh.

395
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:12,270
Suddenly I'm seeing him go off to college!

396
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:16,310
We've gotta go. We've got that cab downstairs.

397
00:21:17,270 --> 00:21:18,560
See you later.

398
00:21:18,730 --> 00:21:20,020
- Bye.     - Bye.

399
00:21:20,190 --> 00:21:21,320
- Oh!     - Ha, ha.

400
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:25,490
- Bye.     - Bye.

401
00:21:25,650 --> 00:21:27,530
Bye.

402
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:29,070
Oh.

403
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:40,290
Wow. Look at this nice deep hole I dug. Hey, Bert...

404
00:21:40,460 --> 00:21:42,090
isn't this a nice hole here?

405
00:21:42,250 --> 00:21:43,340
Okay, ahem.

406
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:48,050
Ben, this is the part where Ernie buries Bert in the sand and can't find him.

407
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:53,760
Now, I've looked ahead on the tape, and he does find him again.

408
00:21:54,890 --> 00:21:58,520
But before that happens, there's some rough going for a while.

409
00:21:58,730 --> 00:22:00,810
But I think we can handle it.

410
00:22:01,060 --> 00:22:06,190
And there's just the alphabet, but we know that ends well, so...

411
00:22:06,570 --> 00:22:07,740
Here we go.

412
00:22:07,950 --> 00:22:09,320
Bert? Bert?

413
00:22:09,490 --> 00:22:11,200
Bert?

414
00:22:11,370 --> 00:22:14,990
What happened to my friend Bert? He was here just a moment ago.

415
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:17,290
Oh, no! My old friend Bert is lost.

416
00:22:17,460 --> 00:22:19,540
- Mm.     - I'm so glad you're here.

